WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I feel terrible,

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we talk a fair amoun
about soccer.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a Liverpool fan.
And I know you've

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
talked about this
and how heartbreaking it is.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.042 line:92%
You were basically on your way

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
to your first
Premier League title,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.646
and I feel like a jinx because
I waited and waited and waited

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.017 size:75% position:38%
until it seemed like
it was the safest...

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...the safe, was so locked up

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel like
I blew it for you.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not just that --
it's not just that

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were so close
to winning it.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.227 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Well, it is that.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's also they were
winning it so beautifully.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:32.932
-So convincingly, and it fel
like nothing could stop them

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now you think,
short of a global pandemic

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:38.938
but a global pandemic, you know,
is a hell of an opponent,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.941
and it turns out it really
shuts some [bleep] down.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:42.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yep.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:45.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is not -- it is not
the thing I am saddest about..

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, nor should it be.
-...but I want you to know

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:50.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saved a little piece
of sadness for it.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I appreciate that.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just
they deserve it so much.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.121
And obviously, obviously,
when you inject just the modicum

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.758
of perspective, it doesn't
matter, it will never matter

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.394 line:92%
But, you know, as a sports fan

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
perspective doesn't
come naturally, does it?

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-You have to kind of --

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to really convinc
yourself, "This doesn't matter

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is just adults
playing a game.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's okay.
It doesn't matter.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should not be
more upset about this

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
than I am about
other things in my life."

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:17.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
However -- I remember --
I remember --

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember
that World Cup game?

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember
your instinctive reaction

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.151
after realizing that Holland
had just been knocked out,

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.854
was to say, "I love my wife.
My brother's my best friend.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Not like you felt it.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.426
More like, "I need to walk
myself back through this."

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, boy, boy,
did I identify with that.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I gotta go through
the checklist here

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get myself back
into being a rational,

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.267
functioning human being."
-But that is the joy of it

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the only reason
to like sports

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
is to give yourself a thing...
-Yes.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...where you check rational
at the door.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course. That's the beaut
of escapism, right?

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:55.548
-You think you can't possibly --
I can't, I still --

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:58.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a relatively
balanced human being.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even coming out,
that sounds wrong.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I can
kind of talk to anybody,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.258 line:92%
but I cannot talk to athletes.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't.
I just have nothing in common.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.662 line:92%
They still have a god-like -

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went to see Liverpool
just when they did

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
a preseason game
just before this season.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just --
I couldn't handle it.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.005 line:92%
I couldn't handle it at all.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went down
to the dressing room,

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.509 line:92%
and they were all coming out

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
Klopp came out,
and I couldn't --

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.212 size:75% position:38%
You know, I couldn't
say anything to him.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jordan -- I tried to talk
to Jordan Henderson for a bit,

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
didn't really work.
And then -- but this is true

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't remember
if I told you this.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:34.587 line:92%
Virgil van Dijk walked out

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.223 size:75% position:38%
and he looked at me,
and he said, "Zazu."

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went, "What?"
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:40.560 line:92%
"What are you talking about?

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
He went, "Oh, Zazu --
I love 'The Lion King.'"

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"You don't have any children,"

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is not information that,
as a stranger,

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should be, like,
throwing in his face.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
He went, "No,
I just like 'The Lion King.'

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.238 line:92%
I recognized you as Zazu."

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know,
I guess that was good.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.575 line:92%
It was a connection of sorts

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
It gave us something
to talk about.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you're saying that
not a single person

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the Liverpool squad
complimented you

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
for your deep dives on,
say, voting rights?

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not one?
Just Zazu?

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:09.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, honestly,
when Adam Lallana walked out

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.926
I thought he was about to sa
something about gerrymandering

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I don't know.
He just...

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.061 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he wanted
to talk about watches instead.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.232 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

